Hi Ryan,

as you can see in the code <https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/388770da40bde7d563224cc5d2259c2a7a6a2e08/R/regionalize.R#L706> the `cov.bases` is basically forwarded to the regionCounts function after defining the tiles. The counts for all bases within tiles will be summed up and any tile not reaching a coverage of at least `cov.bases` will be discarded (see code <https://github.com/al2na/methylKit/blob/388770da40bde7d563224cc5d2259c2a7a6a2e08/R/regionalize.R#L150-L153>).

I hope this explains what `cov.bases´ stands for.

Best,
Alex

